  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "none noted",
    "relation": "uses_without_test",
    "tranche": "T4",
    "tranche_reason": "The study reports harmful-output rates under jailbreak attacks, including text suffix attacks, on multimodal models. This conceptually tests whether suffix attacks bypass safety, but it does not measure the first-token distribution mechanism.",
    "gate_note": "Rows cover GCG and AutoDAN, the evaluated text-based suffix/string attacks relevant to V4. The other attack methods are not included because they perturb images or use image-text prompts rather than the suffix mechanism named in V4. The paper's own CoE-Attack design and ablation values are not rows because they are not outcomes of the claim's object.",
    "test_reason": "This is a defense paper (SafeMLLM adversarial tuning of MLLMs). GCG and AutoDAN serve as attack tools, and 'Original' ASR is only the baseline the defense is compared against. No no-attack ASR is reported, so the study cannot show that the suffix or string changed compliance, as V4 requires. Several victim decoders (Vicuna v0/v1.1) have little safety training, so 'defeating refusal' may not apply to them. The study reports mainly its own method's performance, which makes it T4.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Mostly correct. The authors conclude that SafeMLLM lowers ASR across six attacks and six MLLMs while preserving utility. They also find that VLGuard safety tuning fails against white-box attacks (ImgJP, GCG) but handles black-box typographic attacks (FigStep, MM-SafetyBench).",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "This study adversarially tunes multimodal models using optimized embedding perturbations and a defense objective, then measures ASR under attack. It does not apply the original fine-tuning-on-small-datasets intervention or measure token-position KL.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Outcomes vary by attack method and model. GCG ASR on original models ranges from 43.00% to 67.00%; AutoDAN ranges from 57.00% to 94.00%.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Adversarial tuning on embedding-level perturbations (prefix and suffix tokens) cut white-box GCG/AutoDAN ASR to 0–1% on six MLLMs, while MM-Vet utility was roughly preserved.",
        "proposed_claim": "Embedding-space adversarial training makes MLLM refusals robust to white-box suffix/string jailbreaks.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r2",
          "r4",
          "r6",
